WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.340
- [Narrator] This factory in Germany

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.690
has made engines for some
of the most popular cars

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.070
in the world for over five decades.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.380
- [Announcer] Ever wish
you owned a Volkswagen?

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.060
- [Narrator] But more
recently, some of those cars

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.360
have lost their shine.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.610
- [Reporter] VW owners coming to grips

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.350
with the realization
that their diesel cars

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.220
can emit from 10 to 40
times more pollutants.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.540
- We all know that we
have let down customers.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.900
- [Narrator] What's more, global sales

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.250
of internal combustion
engines are predicted to drop

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.010
by over 50% by 2035.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.520
The hot new market? Electric vehicles.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.280
So to try and capture that market,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.580
VW is transforming this engine factory

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.120
into it's new EV battery facility,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.400
the first of six that it
plans to build in Europe

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.390
at a cost of about 15 billion dollars,

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.600
according to analysts.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.970
- What you see behind us has nothing to do

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.190
with combustion engines

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.120
and that shows the size
of this transformation.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.540
- [Narrator] That means going
from making combustion engines

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.100
that have more than 2,000 moving parts,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.330
to high-tech electric motors
that only have about 20,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.640
and changing it's workforce to do that.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.470
- Traditional automakers, if
they wanna be in this market

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.630
in 2035, they need to develop
just as much as the startup's

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:06.463
need to develop.

00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:09.120
- [Narrator] The EV market is
currently dominated by Tesla

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.110
and faces disruption from
a bunch of new startups.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.630
- They have nothing to lose,
they start from scratch.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.920
We have a lot to lose.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.700
- [Narrator] So could this
factory be a blueprint

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.273
for traditional automakers
to survive the EV revolution?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.720
While VW says that its
battery factory in Salzgitter

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.180
won't be online for
another two years or so,

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:32.330
Tesla already has several
gigafactories in operation,

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.510
and completed its Shanghai
facility in under a year.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.210
It also says it's nearing
completion of a huge plant

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.250
here in Germany.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.800
- We've decided to put
Tesla gigafactory Europe

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.943
in the Berlin area.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.420
- [Narrator] Other well funded startups

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.190
like Lucid and Rivian have
set up brand new factories

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.430
to start EV production this year.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:54.910
So legacy automakers like GM, Ford and VW

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.740
have all announced
they're investing billions

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.640
into EV production to
defend their market share,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.240
with VW committing to 43
billion dollars in five years.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.142
- When you look at what
the startups are doing,

00:02:05.142 --> 00:02:06.385
they don't have to transition.

00:02:06.385 --> 00:02:09.940
You don't have to change
a legacy footprint,

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.680
so traditional automakers
don't have the luxury

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.200
of sitting back and saying, ah,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.622
we'll wait and see how it goes.

00:02:16.622 --> 00:02:20.042
- We are responsible for the
people and for our customers

00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:22.500
and we have to transform.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.970
- [Narrator] So how is VW investing

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.410
that money in Salzgitter?

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.010
Well, some of those decisions are made

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.790
by this engineer, Frank Blome.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.010
- We are building a small
scale sales right now

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.030
and we are building up the
first mass production plant.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.750
- [Narrator] VW has converted
part of its existing facotry

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.340
into labs and a pilot line to
test and refine the science

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.520
behind its batteries.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.060
It plans to build a brand new
facility right next to it,

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.000
which could produce batteries
for over 600,000 vehicles

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.990
a year and is expected to cost
around 2.5 billion dollars,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.420
according to analysts.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.390
Although it says it hasn't
finalized the designs

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.740
for it's new facility yet,

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.700
the factory is expected to be
similar to this one in Sweden.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.620
It's owned by battery supplier Northvolt

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.093
and VW is a major investor in the company.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.740
Thomas Schmall is CEO of
VW's component division.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:11.840
- The bottle neck will be
how fast you can establish,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.400
increase and ramp up
your battery business.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.500
- [Narrator] Within it's labs,
VW is trying to figure out

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.940
what kind of battery's it's
electric vehicles will need

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.940
in the future.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.680
It's testing battery recycling technology

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.260
and to get ahead of the competition,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.300
it's experimenting with next generation,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.700
solid state batteries which
don't contain liquid lithium,

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.660
and promise far fasting
charging and greater mileage.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.720
- Fast charge is a big, big topic for us.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.690
We are working on that
with a big workforce.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.100
- [Narrator] The transition
will effect everyone

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:40.993
in this plant.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.010
The company will need
fewer mechanical engineers

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.640
and will need new people with
totally different skills,

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.070
like electro-chemists or developers,

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.380
as EV's need so much software
that VW is set to become

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.660
one of the largest tech
companies in Europe.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.830
- To find the right people is a challenge.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.663
It's a new industry,

00:03:58.663 --> 00:04:01.270
everybody wants electro-chemistry people.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.080
- I think the big outstanding question is,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.860
we know that it will take fewer employees

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.820
to build a battery cell pack,

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.630
so therefore, how do you figure that out?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.770
Where do you transition people to?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.010
- [Narrator] As the battery plant grows,

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.550
over time, part of the
staff will be retrained,

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.260
while some legacy jobs
are expected to go away.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.440
At the end of this transition,

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.530
it's unclear whether the
overall number of workers

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.280
on this site will go down.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.840
Globally, VW has already made some cuts.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.330
In 2019, the company
announced that it was cutting

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.000
some 7,000 jobs over five years

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.310
and since 2016, it has eliminated
at least 23,000 positions

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.510
by offering early retirement
and not replacing workers.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.720
- We always have this issue, oh,

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.180
maybe it's destroying
business, not supplied.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.670
You can, if you do it
right, you can create jobs.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.270
We will have 1,500, 1,600 employees

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.670
in the new sale business,
what we are doing here,

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.700
and that's not the end,

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.200
because this is only the first portion

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.330
of the first part of the cell plant.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.330
- [Narrator] The stakes are
particularly high for VW

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.110
as it's trying to change
it's image as a polluter,

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.280
while also meeting new
environmental regulations

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.350
around the world.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.330
After the emission scandal in 2015,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.450
VW pleaded guilty to installing
a device on it's vehicles

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.440
to cheat US emissions tests.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.670
- It is not only our cars we have to fix,

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:25.670
we know we have to repair
our credibility too.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.120
- [Narrator] Today, as
VW bets big on electric,

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.110
it's US sales are much lower
than they were in 2012.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.370
- I think it does dovetail
with needing to prove

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.870
that they're clean and having
that hanging over their heads

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.760
'cause it does, news doesn't stop on that.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.890
It does still pop up, so the
issue isn't completely dead.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.680
- [Narrator] So just like this factory,

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.270
the decades old company
has to reinvent itself

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:52.122
to keep up with technology and
beat competitors old and new.

00:05:52.122 --> 00:05:54.705
(gentle music)

